  "qualifications": [
    {
      "source_refs": ["p0024#3"],
      "reason": "The existing wood-breaking activity stays in prose, not an exercise. Adult handling and splinter/fragment precautions prevent an unsafe invitation to force a thick stick by hand."
    },
    {
      "source_refs": ["p0024#4"],
      "reason": "The gas-versus-condensed-matter statement is scoped to the simplified molecular model, not all substances under every conceivable condition. Attraction, stable arrangements and resistance to indefinite interpenetration are retained; electron-shell overlap is not denied."
    },
    {
      "source_refs": ["p0024#5"],
      "reason": "Electrons, nuclei, neutral molecules, strong short-distance electrical interactions and the complexity of internal motion remain. A minimal quantum-theory qualification avoids presenting repulsion as only fixed-charge electrostatics; no quantum formula or extra task is introduced."
    },
    {
      "source_refs": ["p0024#6", "p0024#8"],
      "reason": "The source footnote's signed projection is made explicit: repulsive magnitude minus attractive magnitude gives the signed net component along the line of centers. Magnitudes and directions are not conflated."
    },
    {
      "source_refs": ["p0024#7"],
      "reason": "Repulsion growing faster than attraction is scoped to the model's close-approach range, retaining the especially steep increase at electron-shell overlap rather than asserting monotonic attraction at all distances."
    },
    {
      "source_refs": ["p0025#1", "p0025#4"],
      "reason": "The three source-described curve identities and all signs and limits remain. The molecular-radius sum is an approximate equilibrium-distance description in this schematic model, not an exact universal contact rule."
    },
    {
      "source_refs": ["p0025#5"],
      "reason": "Compression and stretching still produce restoring forces. Return is limited to small, recoverable elastic deformation near equilibrium; there is no claim that arbitrary far-separated molecules or a broken body globally restore themselves."
    },
    {
      "source_refs": ["p0025#6"],
      "reason": "The source's several-molecular-sizes quantity and short-range concept remain. Negligibility is scoped to this neutral-molecule model and is distinguished from an abrupt finite-distance cutoff."
    },
    {
      "source_refs": ["p0025#7"],
      "reason": "The local straight-line approximation concerns the signed net restoring force near equilibrium, not exact linear growth of each component over the whole curve. The thick segment, proportional elastic-force magnitude and failure at larger molecular displacement remain."
    },
    {
      "source_refs": ["p0025#8"],
      "reason": "The source's million-times molecular-size comparison remains a total length deformation distributed across many neighboring layers. Each layer's distance change must stay small and the deformation elastic; the text does not claim every pairwise distance changes equally or arbitrarily large strain obeys Hooke's law."
    }
